# Corpus tooling
# The normalised corpus (data/corpus/) is committed on purpose: it is what makes
# seeding reproducible and reviewable in a diff. The raw markup it was parsed
# from is not, because it is bulky and can be re-fetched with `make corpus-refresh`.
data/wiki_cache/

# Evaluation tooling
# The question set (data/eval/questions.jsonl) is committed: it is the fixture the
# harness reads. Reports are produced by `make eval` and are not tracked.
data/eval/report*.json

# Tooling
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
